(6527545, 969675, 41337, '<td valign="top">I really like the light and her expression you capture. Although there''s nothing wrong with the composition, I do think I would have preferred the scene to include more of the room (i.e. zoomed out) The reason being, more shadows = more fear. However, that''s just me.</td>', 'I really like the light and her expression you capture. Although there''s nothing wrong with the composition, I do think I would have preferred the scene to include more of the room (i.e. zoomed out) The reason being, more shadows = more fear. However, that''s just me.', '2011-09-04 15:56:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527550, 970570, 41337, '<td valign="top">Not sure what this is but it''s pretty expressive when you let your eyes adjust to the rendering.</td>', 'Not sure what this is but it''s pretty expressive when you let your eyes adjust to the rendering.', '2011-09-04 15:59:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527551, 969506, 51379, '<td valign="top">It almost looks like the weather here this week. The composition and content here are likely my favorites of all time. I love the mill and the stacked fences, and the vines up the side of the building. flat water with reflections always imparts a calm mood. This is very well photographed.</td>', 'It almost looks like the weather here this week. The composition and content here are likely my favorites of all time. I love the mill and the stacked fences, and the vines up the side of the building. flat water with reflections always imparts a calm mood. This is very well photographed.', '2011-09-04 16:00:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527554, 970005, 108580, '<td valign="top">Lovely conversion to B&amp;W. Left me wondering what exactly it is despite the clue in the BG. I thought brake lever but it''s a brake mechanism? No Vote due pre-challenge assistance. Hope it fares well Steve despite it''s DPC FS non conformism :) Because I enjoy thought provoking well conceptualised technical images and the quality B&amp;W conversion I''d have given at least a FS 7.</td>', 'Lovely conversion to B&W. Left me wondering what exactly it is despite the clue in the BG. I thought brake lever but it''s a brake mechanism? No Vote due pre-challenge assistance. Hope it fares well Steve despite it''s DPC FS non conformism :) Because I enjoy thought provoking well conceptualised technical images and the quality B&W conversion I''d have given at least a FS 7.', '2011-09-04 16:10:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527555, 970059, 62357, '<td valign="top">Lovely.</td>', 'Lovely.', '2011-09-04 16:12:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527557, 970233, 108580, '<td valign="top">You sure get around...I''m familiar with Clark(e) but I''m not familiar with the background of your travels...and the oddity of submitting your motor-home in many challenges.</td>', 'You sure get around...I''m familiar with Clark(e) but I''m not familiar with the background of your travels...and the oddity of submitting your motor-home in many challenges.', '2011-09-04 16:16:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527560, 970412, 108580, '<td valign="top">Fabulous interior image. ''nuff said. 8.</td>', 'Fabulous interior image. ''nuff said. 8.', '2011-09-04 16:23:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527561, 969318, 41337, '<td valign="top">This is a very good portrait. I like the composition, but I do find myself wondering how it would look as a 6x7 portrait instead of landscape... <br/> <br/>That said, the head positioning, POV slightly below eye level, the spill of light in the background to give separation, b/w conversion and exposure are great. It''s all done with subtlety, which allows a little of that authenticity to shine through from your subject.</td>', 'This is a very good portrait. I like the composition, but I do find myself wondering how it would look as a 6x7 portrait instead of landscape...  That said, the head positioning, POV slightly below eye level, the spill of light in the background to give separation, b/w conversion and exposure are great. It''s all done with subtlety, which allows a little of that authenticity to shine through from your subject.', '2011-09-04 16:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527563, 970321, 108580, '<td valign="top">Magnificently detailed image, in part due to the expert lighting and no doubt a deft hand at PP. A FS 8.</td>', 'Magnificently detailed image, in part due to the expert lighting and no doubt a deft hand at PP. A FS 8.', '2011-09-04 16:23:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527565, 970265, 108580, '<td valign="top">Stunning image, superb clarity, colours, gradation and detail. This is no doubt doing well as DPC eye-candy seascapes do. Front page. The earth curvature is in part due the lens and I guess the norm is flat horizontal? 8</td>', 'Stunning image, superb clarity, colours, gradation and detail. This is no doubt doing well as DPC eye-candy seascapes do. Front page. The earth curvature is in part due the lens and I guess the norm is flat horizontal? 8', '2011-09-04 16:26:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527566, 970058, 108580, '<td valign="top">Powerful. Crisp and Colourful despite the charcoal beach. I''ll stick my neck out and say 10-20 Sigma, 11-16 or 12-24 Tokina? Creatively used those UWA''s are just so much fun and you have certainly had that with this shot. Looking forward to seeing it on or near the front page. A FS 8.</td>', 'Powerful. Crisp and Colourful despite the charcoal beach. I''ll stick my neck out and say 10-20 Sigma, 11-16 or 12-24 Tokina? Creatively used those UWA''s are just so much fun and you have certainly had that with this shot. Looking forward to seeing it on or near the front page. A FS 8.', '2011-09-04 16:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527567, 969487, 108580, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot. Smooth and appealing. Great gradations and simple colours, one of my favourite styles of sunset ''scape photography. A tad vignetting top L and R. A FS 8.</td>', 'Lovely shot. Smooth and appealing. Great gradations and simple colours, one of my favourite styles of sunset ''scape photography. A tad vignetting top L and R. A FS 8.', '2011-09-04 16:30:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527568, 969957, 108580, '<td valign="top">Now that''s photography...A Free Study 9.</td>', 'Now that''s photography...A Free Study 9.', '2011-09-04 16:31:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527569, 970379, 108580, '<td valign="top">Some architecture just lends itself to B&amp;W. This is one of them. Ghostly moment in time, nice work.</td>', 'Some architecture just lends itself to B&W. This is one of them. Ghostly moment in time, nice work.', '2011-09-04 16:31:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527571, 970226, 108580, '<td valign="top">LOL where''s the rest of his body? Lovely image, well cropped and composed. Sharp and only 2 main colours.</td>', 'LOL where''s the rest of his body? Lovely image, well cropped and composed. Sharp and only 2 main colours.', '2011-09-04 16:31:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527572, 969524, 108580, '<td valign="top">Super detailed and crisp DOF. Never mind the eyes, the lips aren''t half bad either. Fab sensual "portrait". A Free Study 8.</td>', 'Super detailed and crisp DOF. Never mind the eyes, the lips aren''t half bad either. Fab sensual "portrait". A Free Study 8.', '2011-09-04 16:31:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527575, 969760, 108580, '<td valign="top">Super image. Great POV and composition. PP a bit heavy for me but it makes the wood texture pop. Musty, rich goodness. I''m familiar with cellars, go at least once a year to the Cape Winelands in South Africa and get a few cases :)</td>', 'Super image. Great POV and composition. PP a bit heavy for me but it makes the wood texture pop. Musty, rich goodness. I''m familiar with cellars, go at least once a year to the Cape Winelands in South Africa and get a few cases :)', '2011-09-04 16:37:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6527611, 970538, 108580, '<td valign="top">Cute. She''s not bad either...except for the nose job :) On a more photographic note, what colour did you pull out to get that aqua tone? Super lighting and skin tone.</td>', 'Cute. She''s not bad either...except for the nose job :) On a more photographic note, what colour did you pull out to get that aqua tone? Super lighting and skin tone.', '2011-09-04 17:12:27.000000', NULL, 1),
