(6531653, 965459, 79625, '<td valign="top">I absolutely LOVE this image.  It could be partly because I''m partial to Mantises since I keep one as a pet.  However, the colors are awesome and the premise is very cool.  I wish for a touch more DOF in the Mantis.  I am not certain it would be an improvement, but I would be interested to see the flower/Mantis were to the right of the image as opposed to the left as something very, very slight in the composition is leaving me uncomfortable.  The blue in the background could pop more as it would contrast nicely to the orange, but that may distract from the insect, so I''m not certain that would be an improvement either, but maybe something to play with.  Extremely nice image as is, however.</td>', 'I absolutely LOVE this image.  It could be partly because I''m partial to Mantises since I keep one as a pet.  However, the colors are awesome and the premise is very cool.  I wish for a touch more DOF in the Mantis.  I am not certain it would be an improvement, but I would be interested to see the flower/Mantis were to the right of the image as opposed to the left as something very, very slight in the composition is leaving me uncomfortable.  The blue in the background could pop more as it would contrast nicely to the orange, but that may distract from the insect, so I''m not certain that would be an improvement either, but maybe something to play with.  Extremely nice image as is, however.', '2011-09-07 13:20:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6531655, 970387, 79625, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous use of color here.  Very ethereal.  Since the foreground rock are out of focus but add to the image, I would suggest cropping about the bottom half of them out.  That stops them from attempting to compete with the sky as a focal point, but still grounds the image.</td>', 'Gorgeous use of color here.  Very ethereal.  Since the foreground rock are out of focus but add to the image, I would suggest cropping about the bottom half of them out.  That stops them from attempting to compete with the sky as a focal point, but still grounds the image.', '2011-09-07 13:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
