(6533259, 970042, 134665, '<td valign="top">Should have been number 1, imo, best photo in the competition!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-09-08 11:19:35.</i></td>', 'Should have been number 1, imo, best photo in the competition!', '2011-09-08 12:18:26.000000', '2011-09-08 12:19:35.000000', 0),
(6533262, 968836, 113884, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RayEthier:</b></div><hr/><i> Actually no... it''s the Neuschwanstein Castle in Schwangau Germany.  I am trying to figure out what vantage point you had to take this image since it does not look like you were standing on the "passerelle" at the rear of the castle.  Nice to see that the scaffolding is finally down.  I am looking forward to visiting this location again in 2013.<br/> <br/>Great image and I wish you the very best of luck in the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes indeed it is the Neuschwanstein Castle. The image was taken from the Marienbrücke bridge.</td>', 'Originally posted by RayEthier: Actually no... it''s the Neuschwanstein Castle in Schwangau Germany.  I am trying to figure out what vantage point you had to take this image since it does not look like you were standing on the "passerelle" at the rear of the castle.  Nice to see that the scaffolding is finally down.  I am looking forward to visiting this location again in 2013. Great image and I wish you the very best of luck in the challenge.   Yes indeed it is the Neuschwanstein Castle. The image was taken from the Marienbrücke bridge.', '2011-09-08 12:25:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6533267, 970092, 119747, '<td valign="top">Wow 12 seconds hand held! Very well done!</td>', 'Wow 12 seconds hand held! Very well done!', '2011-09-08 12:30:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6533270, 968544, 30982, '<td valign="top">Love the story - thank you for sharing it!  Congratulations on the ribbon as well.</td>', 'Love the story - thank you for sharing it!  Congratulations on the ribbon as well.', '2011-09-08 12:36:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6533274, 965763, 58430, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> I absolutely love this!  It is not blown out on my monitor, nor do I think it too soft - just right as far as I''m concerned.  GREAT shot! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, on my monitor it is sharp and not blown out.  I think the issue is with other member''s monitors.  Mine is a huge beautiful iMac that is calibrated.  If you zoom into the actual pixel size it is tack sharp and not blown out.<br/> <br/>Thank you, Deb!  Your comments are always more valuable than any score in a challenge :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: I absolutely love this!  It is not blown out on my monitor, nor do I think it too soft - just right as far as I''m concerned.  GREAT shot!   Yeah, on my monitor it is sharp and not blown out.  I think the issue is with other member''s monitors.  Mine is a huge beautiful iMac that is calibrated.  If you zoom into the actual pixel size it is tack sharp and not blown out. Thank you, Deb!  Your comments are always more valuable than any score in a challenge :-)', '2011-09-08 12:42:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6533285, 970321, 30982, '<td valign="top">Only one vote below 5 and a whopper of a commenter average!  Most importantly, though, is an amazing, perfect fairy tale picture.  It simply could not be any better.  A wonderful gift to the couple!</td>', 'Only one vote below 5 and a whopper of a commenter average!  Most importantly, though, is an amazing, perfect fairy tale picture.  It simply could not be any better.  A wonderful gift to the couple!', '2011-09-08 12:56:43.000000', NULL, 0),
